{
  "_comment": "Federal Court of Australia judicial review data, keyed by ACCC merger_id. Each value is a LIST of records, one per Federal Court file (a bare record is still read as a list of one, but write lists). Hand-maintained fields: applicant (who sought the review), filed_date (bare ISO 'YYYY-MM-DD'), case_number (the Federal Court file number, e.g. 'NSD1310/2026'), case_url (the file's Commonwealth Courts Portal page, e.g. https://www.comcourts.gov.au/file/Federal/P/nsd1310/2026/actions), and optionally status ('current' | 'concluded'), outcome (withdrawn / dismissed / set_aside — see scripts/constants/judicial_review.py) and concluded_date, which override what is derived from the portal. The 'portal' block is written by scripts/scrape/scrape_federal_court.py (the 'Scrape Tribunal' workflow) from the portal: file details, and per application its listings (with orders and judgments, mirrored under data/raw/matters/{merger_id}/ and recorded as url_gh), its documents filed and its parties (with contact details, which are not published to the site). Do not edit 'portal' by hand except to drop a document filed for good: they are merged additively. A record without a 'portal' block (not yet scraped) still renders from the hand fields. Merged into the frontend data by scripts/generate/static_data (loaders.load_judicial_reviews and enrichment.link_judicial_reviews): while any file is current the merger is 'under judicial review'; every document filed, order, judgment and past court listing becomes a timeline event, and upcoming hearings are upcoming events.",
